<!--
  Sprint 28 (C1, audit round 6): a level JDT ACCEPTS that the previous shape
  check refused. javap on the shipped JDT jar declares VERSION_1_1..VERSION_1_8
  and VERSION_9..VERSION_27; the round-4 bound was `1\.[3-8]|[9]|[1-4][0-9]`,
  which accepted 28-49 (impossible) and refused 1.1 and 1.2 (real).

  Ancient, and that is the point: the bound must come from what JDT declares,
  not from what looks like a reasonable range.
-->
